{"actions":[{"actionCode":"H21000","actionDate":"2025-11-19","source":"House committee actions","text":"Subcommittee Hearings Held","type":"Committee"},{"actionCode":"H11000","actionDate":"2025-11-12","source":"House committee actions","text":"Referred to the Subcommittee on Water, Wildlife and Fisheries.","type":"Committee"},{"actionCode":"H11100","actionDate":"2025-01-13","source":"House floor actions","text":"Referred to the House Committee on Natural Resources.","type":"IntroReferral"},{"actionCode":"Intro-H","actionDate":"2025-01-13","source":"Library of Congress","text":"Introduced in House","type":"IntroReferral"},{"actionCode":"1000","actionDate":"2025-01-13","source":"Library of Congress","text":"Introduced in House","type":"IntroReferral"}],"congress":119,"congressGovUrl":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/house-bill/338","cosponsors":[{"bioguideId":"F000469","fullName":"Rep. Fulcher, Russ [R-ID-1]","isOriginalCosponsor":true,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2025-01-13","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"ID"},{"bioguideId":"V000129","fullName":"Rep. Valadao, David G. [R-CA-22]","isOriginalCosponsor":true,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2025-01-13","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"CA"},{"bioguideId":"G000605","fullName":"Rep. Gray, Adam [D-CA-13]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"D","sponsorshipDate":"2025-01-15","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"CA"},{"bioguideId":"H001090","fullName":"Rep. Harder, Josh [D-CA-9]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"D","sponsorshipDate":"2025-01-15","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"CA"},{"bioguideId":"F000466","fullName":"Rep. Fitzpatrick, Brian K. [R-PA-1]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2025-03-11","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"PA"},{"bioguideId":"S001148","fullName":"Rep. Simpson, Michael K. [R-ID-2]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2025-07-21","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"ID"},{"bioguideId":"M001241","fullName":"Rep. Min, Dave [D-CA-47]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"D","sponsorshipDate":"2025-11-19","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"CA"}],"fetchedAt":"2026-09-16T18:57:55+00:00","id":"hr338-119","introducedDate":"2025-01-13","latestAction":{"actionDate":"2025-11-19","text":"Subcommittee Hearings Held"},"laws":[],"number":"338","originChamber":"House","policyArea":"Water Resources Development","sponsors":[{"bioguideId":"C001059","district":21,"fullName":"Rep. Costa, Jim [D-CA-21]","party":"D","state":"CA"}],"summaries":[{"actionDate":"2025-01-13","actionDesc":"Introduced in House","text":"<p><strong>Every Drop Counts Act</strong></p><p>This bill expands the Bureau of Reclamation's Small Storage Program, which is a grant program for small surface water or groundwater storage projects in certain western states.</p><p>First, the bill expands the types of projects that are eligible for grants under the program. Specifically, the bill makes a project eligible for a grant if the project (1) has water storage capacity of recharges no less than 200 acre-feet and no more than 150,000 acre-feet on an average annual basis over the life of the project for storage or use; and (2) increases groundwater aquifer storage, conveys water to or recovers water from groundwater storage, and stabilizes groundwater levels.</p><p>Next, it extends Reclamation's authority to carry out the grant program for another five years.</p>","updateDate":"2025-04-02T14:26:44Z","versionCode":"00"}],"title":"Every Drop Counts Act","type":"hr","updateDate":"2026-07-18T00:06:20Z","updateDateIncludingText":"2026-07-18T00:06:20Z"}
